of transfer and stability of expression</article-title><source>Hum Gene Ther</source><year>1993</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>151</fpage><lpage>159</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8494924</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B35"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sternberg</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Spizz</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Perry</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name><name><surname>Vizard</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Weil</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Olson</surname><given-names>EN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of upstream and intragenic regulatory elements that confer cell-type-restricted and differentiation-specific expression on the muscle creatine kinase gene</article-title><source>Mol Cell Biol</source><year>1988</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>2896</fpage><lpage>2909</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3405222</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B36"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cao</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruder</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kovesdi</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Huard</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Muscle stem cells can act as antigen-presenting cells: implication for gene therapy</article-title><source>Gene Ther</source><year>2004</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>1321</fpage><lpage>1330</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15175641</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.gt.3302293</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B37"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weeratna</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><nam